!Sample_source_name_ch1 = contralateral hemisphisphere
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Mus musculus
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 10090
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tissue: contralateral pericyte
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = RNA was isolated using miRNeasy micro Kit (Qiagen).
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Approx. 250pg of total RNA was used as input for SMART®-Seq HT Kit (Takara Clontech).
!Sample_description = counts.matrix.norm_anno
!Sample_description = cPC_1
!Sample_data_processing = The resulting raw reads were assessed for quality, adapter content and duplication rates with FastQC.
!Sample_data_processing = Trimmomatic version 0.38 was employed to trim reads after a quality drop below a mean of Q20 in a window of 10 nucleotides. Only reads between 30 and 150 nucleotides were cleared for further analyses.
!Sample_data_processing = Trimmed and filtered reads were aligned versus the Ensembl mouse genome version mm10 (GRCm38) using STAR 2.6.1d with the parameter “--outFilterMismatchNoverLmax 0.1” to increase the maximum ratio of mismatches to mapped length to 10%.
!Sample_data_processing = The number of reads aligning to genes was counted with featureCounts 1.6.3 tool from the Subread package. Only reads mapping at least partially inside exons were admitted and aggregated per gene. Reads overlapping multiple genes or aligning to multiple regions were excluded.
!Sample_data_processing = Differentially expressed genes were identified using DESeq2 version 1.18.1 .
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: mm10
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: library size normalized counts
